WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
Here is the iron thiocyanate tube from earlier,

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.680
settled at ten units of iron three plus,

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.160
ten of thiocyanate and ten of the red

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:08.880
ion.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.520
We add more iron, and it settles again,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.040
at fifteen, eight and twelve.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.320
Every amount has changed.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.160
Yet one thing has not.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.480
Take the red ion, and divide by the

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.680
iron times the thiocyanate.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.000
Ten over ten times ten is a tenth.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.800
Twelve over fifteen times eight is also a

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.920
tenth.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.159
So what is this ratio, why does it

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.080
stay put, and how do we write it

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.360
for any reaction?

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.886
We write a species in square brackets for

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:40.446
its amount per litre.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.246
Now remember the rates.

00:00:42.487 --> 00:00:44.966
In this model, joining runs at point three

00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:48.486
times the iron times the thiocyanate, and splitting

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.806
runs at three times the red ion.

00:00:51.127 --> 00:00:54.246
At equilibrium the rates are equal, so point

00:00:54.327 --> 00:00:58.006
three times iron times thiocyanate equals three times

00:00:58.087 --> 00:00:58.966
the red ion.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:02.806
Divide both sides by three, and by the

00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:05.126
iron times the thiocyanate.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:08.886
The red ion over iron times thiocyanate equals

00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:11.686
point three over three, a tenth.

00:01:11.927 --> 00:01:14.166
Those two numbers are fixed for this reaction

00:01:14.247 --> 00:01:16.886
at one temperature, so the ratio comes out

00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:19.246
the same whenever the rates are equal.

00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:22.566
Chemists give that value a name, the equilibrium

00:01:22.647 --> 00:01:26.166
constant, K, also written Keq.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.926
Now the hydrogen iodide tube from the catalyst

00:01:30.007 --> 00:01:33.766
video, settled at two, two and fourteen, with

00:01:33.887 --> 00:01:35.366
both rates a fifth.

00:01:35.687 --> 00:01:38.246
In this model, joining needs a hydrogen and

00:01:38.327 --> 00:01:40.566
an iodine to meet, so we write it

00:01:40.647 --> 00:01:43.926
as a number times hydrogen times iodine.

00:01:44.007 --> 00:01:46.726
With hydrogen and iodine both at two, a

00:01:46.807 --> 00:01:49.926
fifth means that number is point oh five.

00:01:50.087 --> 00:01:53.126
Splitting needs two hydrogen iodide to meet.

00:01:53.207 --> 00:01:55.446
Like the nitrogen dioxide pairs in the squeeze

00:01:55.527 --> 00:01:58.166
video, that makes the rate depend on hydrogen

00:01:58.247 --> 00:01:59.926
iodide squared.

00:02:00.047 --> 00:02:02.166
With fourteen of them and a fifth, its

00:02:02.327 --> 00:02:05.526
number is point oh five over forty-nine.

00:02:05.607 --> 00:02:08.486
Set the rates equal, and hydrogen iodide squared

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:12.246
over hydrogen times iodine equals forty-nine.

00:02:12.287 --> 00:02:14.886
The coefficient two has become a power of

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:15.446
two.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.986
We have shown why for two reactions.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:22.746
Real reactions are often several smaller steps, but

00:02:22.827 --> 00:02:25.866
measurements on many reactions give the same pattern,

00:02:25.947 --> 00:02:27.306
so we use it as the rule for

00:02:27.387 --> 00:02:30.506
any balanced equation, for the equation exactly as

00:02:30.587 --> 00:02:31.146
given.

00:02:31.387 --> 00:02:34.506
Products go on top, reactants underneath, and each

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.746
concentration is raised to the power of its

00:02:36.827 --> 00:02:37.546
coefficient.

00:02:38.107 --> 00:02:41.546
Our settled tube has two, two and fourteen,

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:44.186
and fourteen squared over two times two is

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.706
a hundred and ninety-six over four, forty-nine.

00:02:47.787 --> 00:02:49.786
A tube that started with more iodine than

00:02:49.867 --> 00:02:53.466
hydrogen settles at two, eight and twenty-eight, and

00:02:53.547 --> 00:02:56.186
twenty-eight squared over two times eight is seven

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:59.386
hundred and eighty-four over sixteen, forty-nine again.

00:03:00.107 --> 00:03:01.786
Leave the power off and you get three

00:03:01.867 --> 00:03:04.826
and a half, then one point seven five,

00:03:04.867 --> 00:03:07.066
so the ratio no longer stays put.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:11.306
Let us write an equilibrium expression, the ratio

00:03:11.387 --> 00:03:14.426
for one equation, from scratch, using the cobalt

00:03:14.507 --> 00:03:15.466
tube.

00:03:15.547 --> 00:03:18.586
The pink cobalt water ion and chloride ions

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.946
make the blue cobalt chloride ion and water.

00:03:22.147 --> 00:03:23.706
First, the states.

00:03:23.947 --> 00:03:27.306
Species in solution have concentrations that change, so

00:03:27.387 --> 00:03:28.506
they go in.

00:03:28.587 --> 00:03:31.146
The water is a liquid, the solvent, so

00:03:31.227 --> 00:03:32.426
it stays out.

00:03:32.627 --> 00:03:35.306
Second, products over reactants.

00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:38.106
Third, each concentration to the power of its

00:03:38.187 --> 00:03:41.386
coefficient, so chloride, with a four in front,

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:43.546
is raised to the fourth power.

00:03:43.587 --> 00:03:46.026
The square brackets go around the whole ion,

00:03:46.107 --> 00:03:48.346
including its own brackets and charge.

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:52.206
Why leave out the solvent, or a solid?

00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:55.286
Because their concentration does not change while the

00:03:55.327 --> 00:03:56.646
reaction runs.

00:03:56.927 --> 00:03:59.806
Remember the rate equations: a number times the

00:03:59.887 --> 00:04:00.926
concentrations.

00:04:01.487 --> 00:04:04.286
If one concentration never changes, it is just

00:04:04.447 --> 00:04:06.926
another fixed number, so it folds into the

00:04:07.007 --> 00:04:10.046
fixed numbers we already have, and K already

00:04:10.287 --> 00:04:10.766
includes it.

00:04:11.407 --> 00:04:13.246
We met this with carbon in the squeeze

00:04:13.327 --> 00:04:16.046
video, which squeezing could not make any more

00:04:16.127 --> 00:04:17.086
crowded.

00:04:17.207 --> 00:04:19.886
So for carbon plus carbon dioxide making two

00:04:20.047 --> 00:04:23.806
carbon monoxide, K is the carbon monoxide squared

00:04:23.887 --> 00:04:26.846
over the carbon dioxide, and the carbon never

00:04:26.967 --> 00:04:28.206
appears.

00:04:28.287 --> 00:04:30.846
If water is a gas, as steam, its

00:04:30.927 --> 00:04:33.406
concentration changes, so it counts.

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:36.353
What does the number tell us?

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:39.993
K is products over reactants, so the bigger

00:04:40.074 --> 00:04:42.393
it is, the more the settled mixture leans

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:43.753
towards products.

00:04:44.074 --> 00:04:46.233
As a rough guide, a K above about

00:04:46.314 --> 00:04:48.873
a thousand means the mixture at equilibrium is

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:51.673
mostly products, and a K below about a

00:04:51.714 --> 00:04:54.433
thousandth means it is mostly reactants.

00:04:54.714 --> 00:04:57.873
In between, both are present in measurable amounts.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:04:59.913
It is only a rough guide, because it

00:05:00.114 --> 00:05:01.193
depends on the equation.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.993
Hydrogen and iodine at four hundred and fifty

00:05:04.074 --> 00:05:07.593
degrees have a K of forty-nine: in between,

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:09.913
so our tube holds a lot of hydrogen

00:05:09.994 --> 00:05:12.713
iodide, with some hydrogen and iodine left.

00:05:13.354 --> 00:05:16.233
Nitrogen and oxygen making nitric oxide have a

00:05:16.314 --> 00:05:18.233
K near ten to the minus thirty at

00:05:18.314 --> 00:05:21.833
room temperature, so almost no nitric oxide forms.

00:05:22.474 --> 00:05:24.873
Copper ions with plenty of ammonia make a

00:05:25.034 --> 00:05:27.033
deep blue ion with a K near ten

00:05:27.114 --> 00:05:29.993
to the thirteen, so almost all the copper

00:05:30.114 --> 00:05:31.353
ends up in that ion.

00:05:31.994 --> 00:05:34.553
K tells you where the mixture settles, not

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:36.153
how fast it gets there.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:40.006
Here is a shortcut for writing any expression.

00:05:40.487 --> 00:05:45.606
Products over reactants, coefficients become powers, pure solids,

00:05:45.687 --> 00:05:48.246
a pure liquid and the solvent drop out.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:50.106
Your turn.

00:05:50.747 --> 00:05:53.946
Two settled mixtures, each at a steady temperature.

00:05:54.427 --> 00:05:58.026
One: in dilute aqueous solution, copper two plus

00:05:58.187 --> 00:06:01.226
ions and ammonia make a deep blue ion.

00:06:01.707 --> 00:06:03.386
Write the equilibrium expression.

00:06:04.027 --> 00:06:07.786
Two: a made-up reaction in dilute aqueous solution,

00:06:07.907 --> 00:06:10.746
where A and B make C and D,

00:06:10.827 --> 00:06:12.106
each with a one in front.

00:06:12.587 --> 00:06:13.546
Write the expression.

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:16.666
We start with equal concentrations of A and

00:06:16.747 --> 00:06:18.666
B, and no C or D.

00:06:19.227 --> 00:06:21.386
In this question K is four.

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:23.546
What does that tell you about the settled

00:06:23.587 --> 00:06:24.306
mixture?

00:06:24.587 --> 00:06:25.786
Pause here to answer.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:36.600
One.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:39.800
Products on top, reactants underneath.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.000
The new ion goes on top.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.160
Underneath goes the copper ion times the ammonia

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.640
to the power of four, because the coefficient

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.240
four becomes a power.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.440
If you wrote four times the ammonia, remember

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:55.560
a coefficient is a power, not a multiplier.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.560
If you added the concentrations underneath, remember joining

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.200
needs the particles to meet, so the counts

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.160
multiply.

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:04.966
Two.

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:08.326
The products go on top, C times D.

00:07:08.607 --> 00:07:12.046
Underneath go the reactants, A times B.

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:14.686
We started with only A and B, in

00:07:14.807 --> 00:07:15.566
equal amounts.

00:07:16.047 --> 00:07:17.966
A K of four works out to about

00:07:18.047 --> 00:07:20.446
two thirds of the A reacting, so the

00:07:20.607 --> 00:07:23.886
settled mixture holds measurable amounts of all four,

00:07:24.007 --> 00:07:25.726
not almost all products.

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:29.493
So when a question gives an equation, write

00:07:29.574 --> 00:07:33.333
products over reactants, give each concentration the power

00:07:33.374 --> 00:07:36.213
of its coefficient, and leave out pure solids,

00:07:36.294 --> 00:07:38.693
a pure liquid and the solvent.

00:07:38.774 --> 00:07:41.013
When it gives you K, read its size

00:07:41.174 --> 00:07:43.973
first, as a rough guide: above about a

00:07:44.014 --> 00:07:47.973
thousand, mostly products, below about a thousandth, mostly

00:07:48.174 --> 00:07:52.093
reactants, and in between, both in measurable amounts.

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:55.733
Next: when you only know the starting amounts,

00:07:55.814 --> 00:07:57.573
how do you find the settled mixture?

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:00.240
Here are the key notes.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.320
Pause the video if you need more time

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:03.200
to copy them.
